  "interpretation": "Three calibrated headline signals: (1) mean ZVF per method (saturated-prompt regime where zvf-triage has 0 headroom); (2) controller cost_ratio with bootstrap CI on the per-step rollout cost; (3) Pareto table comparing 8 controllers. The hybrid rule combines the Dualformer-Auto shrinkage at the boundary and the zvf-triage escalation at the interior. On the N2 data the regime is almost entirely interior_high (zvf >= 0.70 AND pcd <= 0.20), so the hybrid degenerates to zvf-triage and its cost_ratio matches zvf-triage_0.70 exactly."
